{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1425","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1425","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1425\",\"parent_revision\":\"7bb4feb1eb73d838c06e1ee389015ceb0d68b188\",\"root_revision\":\"a9fb84678c267236325d29aa47387807ab476b95d7fcf9dfacc35a353ce76b1b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Current state**\\n\\nCLAUDE.md defines an \\\"Autonomous Action Boundary\\\" table distinguishing \\\"Act without asking\\\" from \\\"Ask before acting\\\" actions. The `verify` skill checks completeness. The `orchestrator-discipline` plugin enforces context window discipline. However, there is no mechanism to restrict file edits to a specific directory during a debugging session. An agent working on a focused fix in `plugins/development-harness/` can edit files anywhere in the repo without constraint. The `.claude/rules/fix-delegation-discipline.md` enforces reproduction-first methodology but does not restrict edit scope.\\n\\n**Target state**\\n\\nA `/freeze` skill or hook exists that, when activated with a directory path argument, configures a `PreToolUse` hook on `Write` and `Edit` tools. The hook rejects any write/edit operation targeting files outside the specified directory. A `/unfreeze` skill removes the restriction. The restriction is session-scoped (does not persist across sessions). The hook returns a clear error message: \\\"BLOCKED -- edit outside freeze boundary {path}. Run /unfreeze to remove restriction.\\\"\\n\\n**Measurable signal**\\n\\nFile `.claude/skills/freeze/SKILL.md` exists and is registered. A hooks.json entry for the freeze PreToolUse hook exists. When activated with `/freeze plugins/development-harness/`, attempting to Edit a file in `plugins/plugin-creator/` is rejected by the hook. Running `/unfreeze` removes the restriction and the Edit succeeds.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `.claude/skills/freeze/SKILL.md` exists and registers the skill\\n- [ ] `.claude/skills/unfreeze/SKILL.md` exists and registers the skill\\n- [ ] A `.cjs` hook script implements PreToolUse blocking: reads freeze marker at `/tmp/.claude-freeze-{session_id}`, blocks Write/Edit if `file_path` is outside the frozen directory (exit code 2 + stderr message)\\n- [ ] hooks.json (or settings.json) registers the hook with `matcher: \\\"Write|Edit\\\"`\\n- [ ] Activating `/freeze plugins/development-harness/` then attempting to Edit `plugins/plugin-creator/` returns the BLOCKED error\\n- [ ] Running `/unfreeze` removes the marker file and subsequent Edit operations succeed\\n- [ ] Subagents (identified by `data.agent_id` in hook stdin) are also blocked when freeze is active\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **edit-restriction mode (/freeze) for focused debugging** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/gstack.md -- pattern: /freeze edit restriction for focused debugging\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-04)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 confirmed. No existing freeze mechanism anywhere in the codebase. Hook infrastructure is mature with clear blocking patterns (exit code 2).\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Design Decisions\\n\\n1. **Scope**: Project-level skill in `.claude/skills/` (not a plugin). Simpler to implement; the need is project-specific debugging discipline.\\n\\n2. **State mechanism**: Temp file at `/tmp/.claude-freeze-{session_id}` containing the frozen directory path. Written by `/freeze`, deleted by `/unfreeze`. Session ID is available in hook stdin JSON.\\n\\n3. **Subagent behavior**: Subagents ARE blocked \u2014 the intent of freeze is to prevent any edit outside the boundary, including delegated work.\\n\\n4. **Bash tool**: Out of scope for initial implementation. Detecting file-writing bash commands is complex. Cover only `Write|Edit`.\\n\\n5. **Multiple directories**: Single directory only for initial implementation.\\n\\n6. **Skill structure**: Two separate skills (`/freeze` and `/unfreeze`) per repo convention.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nCREATE:\\n- `.claude/skills/freeze/SKILL.md`\\n- `.claude/skills/unfreeze/SKILL.md`\\n- `.claude/hooks/freeze-boundary.cjs`\\n\\nMODIFY:\\n- `.claude/settings.json` \u2014 add PreToolUse hook entry for `freeze-boundary.cjs`\\n\\n### Implementation notes\\n\\n- Copy blocking pattern from `.claude/hooks/validate-delegation.cjs` (sync stdin read, exit 2 + stderr)\\n- Copy path inspection pattern from `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/pre-tool-orchestrator-read-warning.cjs` (file_path extraction)\\n- Hook must handle both `Write` (tool_input.file_path) and `Edit` (tool_input.file_path)\\n- If no marker file exists, hook exits 0 immediately (freeze not active)\\n- Error message: `BLOCKED \u2014 edit outside freeze boundary: {frozen_dir}. Run /unfreeze to remove restriction.`\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nIn scope:\\n- `.claude/skills/freeze/SKILL.md` \u2014 writes marker file with frozen path\\n- `.claude/skills/unfreeze/SKILL.md` \u2014 deletes marker file\\n- `.claude/hooks/freeze-boundary.cjs` \u2014 PreToolUse blocking hook\\n- Register in `.claude/settings.json` under `PreToolUse` with `matcher: \\\"Write|Edit\\\"`\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- Bash tool file-write detection\\n- Multi-directory support\\n- Plugin packaging\\n\",\"digest\":\"c1d01ab3b384ba9d4b5804868891fcad81c9f8d51cab4503db179a58426e61a6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg5CKQ\"}"}